Year = {2011},
Number = {2896},
Pages = {53-64},
Month = {MAY 28},
Abstract = {A new species of Riodinidae, Mesene jimena sp. nov., is described from
   the Pacific slope in southern Mexico, including notes on its habits,
   habitat and distribution. A comparison is made with its close relative,
   Mesene margaretta (A. White, 1843), found in southeastern Mexico
   (Atlantic slope) and Chiapas State. In addition to morphology, other
   criteria are discussed including behavior and related structures,
   spatial and temporal factors, comparison of distribution with areas of
   endemism and ecology. These factors were examined for the new taxon and
   found to confirm its status.},
