   (CLAF); SPIE; Div Optica Sociedad Mexicana Fisica (DIVO-SMF); Int Union
   Pure \& Appl Phys (IUPAP)},
Abstract = {This paper shows the qualitative and quantitative results obtained on
   the test of cylindrical parabolic concentrators when the screens are
   designed using dot color changes to guarantee a better dot
   correspondence assignment and to make the optical test of the
   concentrator easier; the method allows to measure deformations from
   tenths of a millimeter to several millimeters, thus demonstrating that
   null screen method is good enough for testing surfaces with important
   deformations. On a second approximation, it is designed a null screen
   corresponding to the surface evaluated with the first one by fitting a
   fourth grade polynomial with crossed terms; with this, it is shown that
   the first test gets closer to the shape of the surface validating it.},
